Maintainer: Brian O'Reilly <fade@deepsky.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: dsmr-qmail-run
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 qmail (>= 1.06.3),
 daemontools-run,
 vpopmail (>= 5.6.13),
 ucspi-tcp6 | ucspi-tcp
Recommends: fastforward
Provides: mail-transport-agent
Conflicts: qmail-run, mail-transport-agent
Replaces: qmail-run, mail-transport-agent
Description: runtime service configuration for the DSMR qmail stack
 Provides supervised service trees for qmail-send, qmail-smtpd (port 25),
 and qmail-submission (port 587 with authentication), along with the
 qmailctl management script and systemd integration via daemontools-run.
 .
 This package makes the DSMR qmail stack the system's mail-transport-agent:
 installing it removes the default Debian MTA (Exim) and provides the standard
 /usr/sbin/sendmail, a best-effort mailq, and a newaliases that rebuilds
 /etc/aliases.cdb via fastforward, so programs that depend on
 "default-mta | mail-transport-agent" are satisfied by qmail.
 .
 On install, this package:
  - Removes the old qmail-verify service (not used by this stack)
  - Creates /etc/qmail/qmail-{send,smtpd,submission}/ service trees
  - Symlinks services into /etc/service/ for svscan supervision
  - Ensures daemontools-run.service is enabled and active
 .
 Replaces the upstream qmail-run package.
